  "intro": {
    "title": "Book Introduction - II John",
    "html": "<p style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Book Introduction - 2 John</p><p><b>WRITER</b>: The Apostle John. </p><p><b>DATE</b>: Probably A.D. 90. </p><p><b>THEME</b>: Second John gives the essentials of the personal walk of the believer in a day when &quot;many deceivers are entered into the world&quot; (<ref>2Jn 1:7</ref>). The key phrase is &quot;the truth,&quot; by which John means the body of revealed truth, the Scriptures. The Bible as the only authority for doctrine and life, is the believer&rsquo;s resource in a time of declension and apostasy. </p><p>The Epistle in three divisions: </p><p>1. The pathway of truth and love, <ref>2Jn 1:1-6</ref> </p><p>2. The peril of unscriptural ways, <ref>2Jn 1:7-11</ref> </p><p>3. Superscription, <ref>2Jn 1:12-13</ref> </p>",
    "text": "Book Introduction - 2 John WRITER : The Apostle John. DATE : Probably A.D. 90. THEME : Second John gives the essentials of the personal walk of the believer in a day when \"many deceivers are entered into the world\" (2Jn 1:7). The key phrase is \"the truth,\" by which John means the body of revealed truth, the Scriptures. The Bible as the only authority for doctrine and life, is the believer’s resource in a time of declension and apostasy. The Epistle in three divisions: 1. The pathway of truth and love, 2Jn 1:1-6 2. The peril of unscriptural ways, 2Jn 1:7-11 3. Superscription, 2Jn 1:12-13"
  },
  "chapters": {
    "1": {
      "chapter": 1,
      "outlines": null,
      "verses": [
        {
          "verse": 1,
          "text": "The elder unto the elect lady and her children, whom I love in the truth; and not I only, but also all they that have known the truth;",
          "marked_text": "The elder unto the elect lady and her children, whom I love in the truth; and not I only, but also all they that have known the truth;<fn n=\"a\"/><fn n=\"b\"/>",
          "outlines": "II John: Book Introduction - II John.",
          "footnotes": null
        },
        {
          "verse": 2,
          "text": "For the truth’s sake, which dwelleth in us, and shall be with us for ever.",
          "marked_text": "For the truth’s sake, which dwelleth in us, and shall be with us for ever.",
          "outlines": null,
          "footnotes": null
        },
        {
          "verse": 3,
          "text": "Grace be with you, mercy, and peace, from God the Father, and from the Lord Jesus Christ, the Son of the Father, in truth and love.",
          "marked_text": "Grace be with you, mercy, and peace, from God the Father, and from the Lord Jesus Christ, the Son of the Father, in truth and love.",
          "outlines": null,
          "footnotes": null
        },
        {
          "verse": 4,
          "text": "I rejoiced greatly that I found of thy children walking in truth, as we have received a commandment from the Father.",
          "marked_text": "I rejoiced greatly that I found of thy children walking in truth, as we have received a commandment from the Father.",
          "outlines": null,
          "footnotes": null
        },
        {
          "verse": 5,
          "text": "And now I beseech thee, lady, not as though I wrote a new commandment unto thee, but that which we had from the beginning, that we love one another.",
          "marked_text": "And now I beseech thee, lady, not as though I wrote a new commandment unto thee, but that which we had from the beginning, that we love one another<fn n=\"1\"/>.<fn n=\"c\"/><fn n=\"d\"/><fn n=\"e\"/><fn n=\"f\"/><fn n=\"g\"/>",
          "outlines": null,
          "footnotes": [
            {
              "verse": 5,
              "note_idx": 1,
              "keyword": "that we love one another",
              "text": "Law (of Christ), Summary: The new \"law of Christ\" is the divine love, as wrought into the renewed heart by the Holy Spirit Rom 5:5; Heb 10:16 and outflowing in the energy of the Spirit, unforced and spontaneous, toward the objects of the divine love; 2Co 5:14-20; 1Th 2:7; 1Th 2:8. It is, therefore, \" the law of liberty\"; Jas 1:25; Jas 2:12 in contrast with the external law of Moses. Moses’ law demands love,; Lev 19:18; Deu 6:5; Luk 10:27 Christ’s law is love; Rom 5:5; 1Jn 4:7; 1Jn 4:19; 1Jn 4:20 and so takes the place of the external law by fulfilling it; Rom 13:10; Gal 5:14. It is the \"law written in the heart\" under the New Covenant. (See Scofield \" Heb 8:8 \") .",
              "html": "<p><b>that we love one another</b> </p><p>Law (of Christ), Summary: The new &quot;law of Christ&quot; is the divine love, as wrought into the renewed heart by the Holy Spirit <ref>Rom 5:5</ref>; <ref>Heb 10:16</ref> and outflowing in the energy of the Spirit, unforced and spontaneous, toward the objects of the divine love; <ref>2Co 5:14-20</ref>; <ref>1Th 2:7</ref>; <ref>1Th 2:8</ref>. It is, therefore, &quot; the law of liberty&quot;; <ref>Jas 1:25</ref>; <ref>Jas 2:12</ref> in contrast with the external law of Moses. Moses&rsquo; law demands love,; <ref>Lev 19:18</ref>; <ref>Deu 6:5</ref>; <ref>Luk 10:27</ref> Christ&rsquo;s law is love; <ref>Rom 5:5</ref>; <ref>1Jn 4:7</ref>; <ref>1Jn 4:19</ref>; <ref>1Jn 4:20</ref> and so takes the place of the external law by fulfilling it; <ref>Rom 13:10</ref>; <ref>Gal 5:14</ref>. It is the &quot;law written in the heart&quot; under the New Covenant. </p><p><i>(See Scofield &quot;</i><i><ref>Heb 8:8</ref></i><i>&quot;)</i>. </p>",
              "references": [
                "Rom 5:5",
                "Heb 10:16",
                "2Co 5:14-20",
                "1Th 2:7",
                "1Th 2:8",
                "Jas 1:25",
